cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Exu: a toolkit for calibrated decision models"
abstract: >-
  An agnostic base for training encoder-only models that answer typed questions
  with probability distributions instead of generated text. The training reward
  is a strictly proper scoring rule, so honest probabilities are the optimum of
  the objective. Implements RLCD, the method TypeSafe introduced for its System
  One models, next to a direct baseline that optimizes the same score without
  sampling. Includes held-out temperature calibration, calibration-aware
  evaluation and an offline inference runtime.
type: software
authors:
